    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Hello, and welcome to NewsHour with me, Sean Lee, live from the BBC World Service in London. Now, tonight is Bill Clinton night at the Democratic National Convention in Chicago, the former president following in the footsteps of his Democratic successor. If that makes sense, Barack Obama addressed the convention on Tuesday, but not before being upstaged by Michelle, his wife. During her speech, Mrs Obama had a dig at one of Donald Trump's regular campaign talking points.",
