    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51298.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "Well, you know, she's put forth that plan. She's put forth a very good plan on housing that will be important to Nevada where we need accessible housing, but the people who are mostly critical are the economists. You put one economist in a room by himself, he'll start an argument. So the public is very much in favor of bringing down inflation with grocery prices. And a lot of its corporate greed, they're decreasing the amount of the product and increasing the cost. And the example I often use is Oreo cookies. They've gotten much thinner. You don't get nearly as much cream between the wafers and you're paying more for it. Nobody wants a skinny Oreo.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
