  {
    "episode_id": 51298,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51298.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "No, certainly not. But let me put to you what was said by the man who chaired the Council of Economic Advisers under President Trump, Kevin Hassett, who's now at Stanford University Tuber Institution. He said, if the government starts to set prices, what inevitably happens is that the price gets set below marginal cost and then supply dries up. In other words, it becomes uncompetitive for retailers to sell the food or indeed for manufacturers to produce it.",
