    "turn_idx": 42,
    "turn_text": "The Moon is believed to have been formed when a Mars-sized object came and hit the planet Earth. the Moon got formed by the material from the Earth and from the bolloid which came and hit the planet Earth. Now in the beginning all this material which was thrown out was in a molten state and therefore we say the lunar magma ocean hypothesis or LMO hypothesis. The lighter material will be floating up whereas the heavier material will be sinking towards the center of the body. What we are finding now with our alpha particle access spectrometer on the rover of the mission is that this composition is fairly same as what has been seen on the high lines by other missions, which in turn tries to validate the lunar magma hypothesis in some sense. But there are subtle differences And one of them is higher abundance of magnitude. Now, if magnesium is higher at the landing site, that means material from the inner part of the moon must have been thrown there. Now, how do we explain this? So we have given the hypothesis that there is a huge crater in the south pole of the moon. Now this basin must have been formed very early in the history of the Moon and the material which have been thrown out from that region from the inner part of the Moon because the basin is quite deep must have brought magnesium at the landing site and therefore this observation also tells us about the history of the evolution of the moon in terms of impacts which it has had in the past.",
