  {
    "episode_id": 51298,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51298.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 50,
    "turn_text": "Basically, after the Taliban took over and there was the evacuation from Kabul, Boris Johnson announced that the UK would take 20,000 refugees from Afghanistan. So we kind of thought it seemed feasible at that point that of those 20,000, 19 would be some of our medical students. At that time, we were supporting 90 Afghan women studying medicine at universities, mostly in Kabul.",
