    "turn_idx": 72,
    "turn_text": "That's Victoria Craig reporting from Turkey. You'll listen to news out from the BBC. I'm Sean Lay here in the BBC World Service Studio in London. Now, let's deal with a situation that's developing as we speak and that is in Sudan after four months. Humanitarian aid has arrived in the country after the Adre border with Chad to the west was finally reopened. It raises hopes that people in Darfur, which was once Sudan's bread basket, can avoid famine. Civil war in the North African countries raged for the past 18 months after the two men who jointly ruled the country fell out with each other. The animosity between General Abdul Fatah Burhan and his rival, General Mohammed Hamdan Daggalo, commander of the Parameletries, the Rapid Support Forces, exploded into open fighting in mid-April 2023. US Special Envoy for Stan is Tom Parello. He gave his reaction to the aid convoy.",
