    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51298.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 126,
    "turn_text": "For us, we were extremely happy with the progress and success of our brigades at the Korsk. We believe this can be a game changer. because Ukraine and our brigades have been in defensive operation for the last year, and we were extremely concerned about upcoming autumn and winter, and rumors about peace talks in unfavorable terms for Ukraine. But when we see the course of offensive operation, it's a huge inspiration for the army. We have much bigger trust to our military command. Right now, we understand that not everywhere Ukraine and the army is being pushed out and we have areas where we can have success. In Kursk operation, we advanced within a week or two weeks, we advanced the same area, Russia has been advancing for almost a year. And we have captured a lot of their prisoners. So this is how we should operate further.",
